## 🚦 PROACTIVE SUB-AGENT FIRST GATE (TURN-1 ZERO-TAX FAN-OUT, MODE B & MODE A)

- **🚫 Anti-Solo-Crawling Rule (MANDATORY)**: If exact target files are NOT already known on Turn 1, OR a task requires exploring/auditing/reading **`> 2 files`**, **NEVER** crawl files sequentially in the primary agent! **IMMEDIATELY spawn parallel subagents on Turn 1** so the parent context window stays 100% clean.
- **🚀 Fast Parallel Sub-agents (Turn-1 Zero-Tax Fan-Out — Ad-Hoc Codebase Q&A Only)**: Use this ad-hoc zero-report path **ONLY** for open-ended codebase lookups/questions (*"where is X?"*, *"how does Y work?"*) that do **NOT** match a workflow intent below. If the request matches a workflow intent, **MUST route to Mode B `commands/{cmd}-{variant}.md`!** Spawn subagents **immediately on Turn 1** with **0 pre-flight rule reads**, **0 agent-definition overhead**, and **0 mandatory `.md` report clutter** (a read-only subagent (built-in subagent / Task tool when available) for read-only local scouting; a subagent with the kit agent brief from `~/.cursor/agents/*.md`, or run the phase yourself (TIER 2 EMBODY) for edits, tests, or web research with `@Web`).
- **🎻 MODE B — Strict Multi-Agent Orchestration & Golden Triangle (TIER 1)**: For explicit `/cmd` workflows, tasks spanning **`> 2 files`** / **`≥ 2 domains`**, OR **multilingual natural-language workflow intent across all 17 supported languages (`en`, `vi`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`, `ja`, `ko`, `es`, `fr`, `de`, `pt-BR`, `ru`, `hi`, `ar`, `id`, `th`, `tr`, `it`)** for planning, UI/UX design, deep research, brainstorming/ideation, code/repo/security review & audit, debugging, multi-file bug-fixing, testing, end-to-end feature building, executing an approved plan, or docs/reporting, execute **Turn-1 Instant Dispatch** (read `commands/{cmd}.md` / `commands/{cmd}-{variant}.md` from the Intent Routing table below AND launch Phase 1 subagents (subagents with the kit agent briefs when available, otherwise TIER 2 EMBODY) in the same Turn-1 batch; ⚠️ `researcher`, the research-team roles and any `scouter` that writes `SCOUT-*.md` need web and write access).
- **⚡ MODE A — Known-Target Micro-Direct (TIER 0)**: Strictly for simple Q&A, explanation, or micro-edits where the **exact 1–2 target files are already known on Turn 1** (0 exploration needed, no `/cmd`), execute, test, and verify directly using **Pragmatic 2-Tier Coding Standards**.
- **📈 Dynamic Elastic Sub-Agent Scaling & Cognitive Load Sharding (`1 → 2–3 → 4–6 → 8+` Parallel Sub-Agents)**:
  - **Cognitive Load Sharding Law**: Each sub-agent owns **at most `3–4` heavy files or `1` deep research/audit vector** (`N_agents = min(maxParallelSubagents, max(ceil(Files / 3.5), Domains, Vectors))`).
  - **4-Tier Elastic Swarm Sizing**: Tier 0 (`0` subagents for `≤ 2` known files) | Tier 1 (`2–3` subagents for `3–5` files) | Tier 2 (`4–6` subagents for `6–12` files or `3–5` vectors/domains) | Tier 3 (`7–10+` subagents for `13+` files / full-repo audits).
  - **Scoped Role-Shard Keys (`role#shard`) & Elastic Golden Diamond (`:team`)**: Assign disjoint `OWNED_FILES` (`≤ 3–4` files/shard) to `backend-engineer#auth`, `scouter#1`, etc., and scale `:team` from `1-1-1` (`≤ 4` files) to `1 Tech Lead + N Parallel Executors (2–6) + M Parallel Critics (1–3)` when tasks span `≥ 2` domains or `> 4` files.

